A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate only when evidence supports the **same cause** as an open ticket
([decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause), replacing decision 0001):

1. Read the report and look up its tenant's locale and form version.
2. Use the input channel and tenant settings to establish its failure path.
3. Merge into a ticket for that cause. Otherwise, open a separate ticket and investigate.

<Callout>
Matching subjects are not enough. Different subjects may share a cause; identical subjects
may describe different causes. Browser locale and intake tags are not tenant settings.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Keep the report separate until its cause is established. Missing tenant data is not evidence
of a duplicate. Flag one-day symptoms for investigation even when the classifier files them as parser.
